WEBVTT

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.590
<i>In the year 2020 C.E.,</i>

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.100
<i>the human world is connected by a network.</i>

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.810
<i>Inhabiting it is
an unknown life form called Digimon.</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.130
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.130
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.220
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.220
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.980
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.980
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.990
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.990
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.200
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.200
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.370
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.370
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.470
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.470
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.690
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.690
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.570
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.570
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.200
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.200
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.280
<i>Darkness has started making its move.</i>

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.280
<i>And the Holy Digimon must stop it.</i>

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.660
<i>As they learn of their mission,</i>

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.040
<i>Taichi's party is targeted
by a swarm of Digimon.</i>

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.720
<i>Danger also closes in on Koshiro
who is moving through the Network.</i>

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.510
<i>At that moment,
Tentomon evolves into Kabuterimon</i>

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.060
<i>and succeeds in protecting Koshiro.</i>

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.580
<i>Taichi's party, who also succeeds
in escaping the attack,</i>

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.670
<i>set out to cross the sea to the continent
where the Holy Digimon awaits.</i>

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.800
Umm...

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.760
Which way is the sea?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.770
THE TARGETED KINGDOM

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:29.480
There's 72 hours until Tokyo comes
to a complete stop.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.020
How long has it been
since he's told me that?

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.780
It's no use. We can't see it anywhere.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.110
Yeah...

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.820
Oh?!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.370
I'm getting hungry too.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.160
Whoa.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.710
Digimon stomachs sure are loud.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.670
I'm starving too!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.010
We need to get food somehow.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.000
Yeah.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.300
I smell something good!

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.430
-Ooh!
-Smells yummy!

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.180
Isn't this...

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.480
They fell for it!

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.450
We got you, fruit thieves!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.950
TANEMON

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.750
Looks like we've been caught.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.460
What are these guys?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.830
They're Tanemon!

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.250
W-Wait! We haven't done anything!

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.720
What? You were trying to steal our fruits!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.510
You caught them?

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.850
Any fruit thieves deserve a punishment!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.440
A human?!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.960
Welcome to Mimi's Kingdom.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.880
Mimi's Kingdom?

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.130
Who in the world are you?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.470
Oh, that's right,
I haven't introduced myself!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:27.260
I'm Mimi Tachikawa, a fourth-grader.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.890
And I'm the queen of this kingdom!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.430
The queen...

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.150
And this is my butler, Palmon!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.100
PALMON

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.230
Hey, all of you!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.440
Are you really not with Tuskmon?!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.320
Tuskmon?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.790
Aren't Tuskmon really rough and big pigs?

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.670
That's true, they're a nasty crowd.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.130
Well, that's fine.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.420
Let's just say
our misunderstanding is cleared.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.420
So, what did you all come here for?

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.930
It's just that we've gotten a little lost.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.390
Lost?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.230
The damages are spreading fast.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.520
And...

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.320
What's this?!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.070
Really, you're looking for
the Holy Digimon?

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:32.330
Oh yeah, I think I heard something
like that while I was taking a nap too.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.200
What?!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.990
Mimi-chan too?

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.370
I think I heard it from this.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.340
Oh!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.220
Mimi-chan is the same as us.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.970
The Chosen Ones?!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.300
The Chosen Ones?

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.230
Oh, no, no!
We don't have time for that right now!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.610
To protect this Mimi's Kingdom,

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.110
I have to fight fruit thieves
day and night!

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.610
That's right! That's our queen!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.490
What?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.950
<i>Taichi-san, emergency!</i>

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.950
Hey, you can use this like a smartphone?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:15.830
Yeah.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.490
What's wrong, Koshiro?

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.590
<i>Please watch this video first.</i>

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:24.840
Video? It's not moving though.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.670
<i>When I tried to watch this news program
from my current location earlier...</i>

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:30.840
Huh?

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.760
Hey, look at this.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.560
This part.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.270
Oh, it's moving slowly!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.520
You're right!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.060
Is this in slow motion?

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.270
<i>No, it's not!</i>

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:49.710
<i>What I can tell from this video is
that time flows at different speeds</i>

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:52.880
<i>between our world and the Digital World.</i>

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.530
Say what?!

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.460
COREDRAMON

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.810
TUSKMON

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.300
Find.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.900
ORGEMON

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.900
The children.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.530
Is that true?!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.950
Time flows differently here
than our world?

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.540
I haven't verified it,
but I'm sure there's no mistake.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.580
What we saw during the incident before

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.730
was only the shallow part of this world.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.590
This region is beyond the knowledge
of mankind who created the Network.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:55.930
The deeper you go, the more lag
in time there is between our worlds.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:01.440
<i>And I believe this Digivice
must have been fixing that lag</i>

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.690
<i>to enable two-way communication.</i>

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:09.320
So, Koshiro, about that time difference...

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:12.990
Since the video from the other side
looks slow, that means...

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.200
<i>Yes.</i>

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.450
<i>From the Digital World
where all of you are right now,</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:20.660
DIGITAL WORLD
TOKYO

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.700
<i>time in our world is moving slowly.</i>

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.000
So Mimi-chan sounds
like she's been here for long,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.340
but she was actually transported to this
world just a little while before us then.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.380
That may be true...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:37.620
We now know that we have
more time than we thought.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.680
But...

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.890
<i>Yes, we cannot be taking our time.</i>

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.480
<i>Please take a look at this.</i>

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.850
<i>I've encoded that news video
so that you can watch it on your side.</i>

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.110
Hm? Is that about our town?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.400
<i>The unknown major power failure
is continuing to grow currently.</i>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.450
<i>The government has set
mobile power supply cars</i>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:05.500
<i>at hospitals, broadcasting stations,
and other essential facilities.</i>

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:06.960
Oh...

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.000
Hm?

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>As you can see, the damages
are continuing to spread even now.</i>

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.380
Tokyo...

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.180
I didn't know Tokyo was in this state.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:24.270
<i>The mobile power supply cars seem to be
lent out by certain companies for free.</i>

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh, Grandpa!

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.350
Grandpa?

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:32.560
I'm sure that man is the chairman
of Tachikawa Heavy Industries.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.570
Chairman?!

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.280
<i>It isn't about company profits.</i>

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:42.400
<i>I'm just doing what I can do right now.</i>

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.950
Grandpa...

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.540
What I can do...

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:50.290
Oh!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.290
It disappeared...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.800
Grandpa is working so hard.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.510
But...

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.640
Right now...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.560
I have these little guys, my kingdom.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:14.520
Protecting them
from bad guys is what's most important!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.570
That's right! That's our kingdom's queen!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.820
Say, Mimi-chan.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.580
No, Queen Mimi!

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.450
Let us join you too!

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.290
We'll get rid of those guys with you!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.040
What?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.130
Let us help you too!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.590
Yeah, yeah, leave it to us!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.210
I'll fight too!

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.130
All of you...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.220
For my kingdom?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.220
We gotta do what we can, right?

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.300
Then you're No. 72!

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.100
Huh?

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.230
You're No. 73!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.110
What?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:59.690
I'll make you all servants
of Mimi-chan's Kingdom!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:27.850
They're here!

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.600
So, six Tuskmon!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.230
We'll haul in the fruit thieves
for sure this time!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.150
Go!

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:50.580
Yes!

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.000
First, we got two!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.750
It went well!

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.050
They're going around the rocks
to avoid the traps!

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.510
All right, let's go, Agumon!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:06.680
Okay!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.430
We're counting on you!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.110
Agumon!

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.820
Leave it to me!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.930
Agumon Evolution!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.980
Greymon!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.910
Greymon!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.670
Mega Flame!

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.420
Sounds like it's started!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.380
Hm?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.630
I wonder what that is?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:28.760
Piyomon!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.720
Okay!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.850
Two left!

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.310
Greymon!

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:49.360
Huh?!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.910
That's...

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:57.370
Meteor Wing!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.630
Birdramon!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.260
Go, Birdramon!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.730
I leave that guy to you!

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:28.570
Are you scared?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.450
What?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.570
Just a little...

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:37.370
Don't worry, I'll protect you, Mimi.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.200
Yeah!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.680
W-What is it?!

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.600
We won't let you steal our fruits!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.940
DRIMOGEMON

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.450
Palmon...

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.830
Children...

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.960
Run, Mimi...

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.710
Palmon?!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.640
Mimi!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.360
Palmon!

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.870
Just one left!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.550
We're done here!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.090
Nice!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.510
Looks like she took the best part...

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.390
Palmon!

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.220
Palmon?!

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.860
Mimi...

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.790
You can't be here...

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.070
Palmon!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:34.320
Their target is you, Mimi...

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.950
Palmon...

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.450
The Chosen... Ones...

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.450
So run, please...

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.250
I can't just leave you here and run.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.460
How could I?!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.130
<i>When I arrived here
and was lonely all by myself,</i>

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.090
<i>you came over to talk to me.</i>

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.850
<i>And you introduced me to Tanemon
to make us friends.</i>

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.810
It's all thanks to you, Palmon.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.730
Mimi...

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.780
That's why I can't run away by myself!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.270
Mimi...

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.190
What?

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.570
What is... this?

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.450
Hm?!

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.390
Palmon Evolution!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.900
TOGEMON

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.950
Togemon!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.660
Togemon...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.410
Palmon has changed.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.740
So this is an evolution!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.580
Evolution...

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.090
Move!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.890
Mimi-chan!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.640
Greymon!

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.080
Yes!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.250
But look...

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.170
Togemon!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.140
Wow! Go, Togemon!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.060
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.230
Coconut...

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:17.400
Upper!

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.490
It's a knockout!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.400
Mimi-chan!

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:29.700
You okay?!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.000
Oh...

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.010
Palmon, thank you.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:41.260
I'm glad you're okay, Mimi!

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.470
Palmon!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.470
Mimi!

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:52.020
I love you, Palmon!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:56.110
I love you too, Mimi!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.680
Are you really sure about this?

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:24.550
Yeah.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.310
<i>We got rid of the bad guys
who attacked the village...</i>

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:37.980
<i>and since Tanemon say they'll protect
the kingdom themselves.</i>

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:42.990
I'm...

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.280
going to do what I can right now!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:47.530
Yup!

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:07.280
<i>As if rolling out of control,
I ran frantically</i>

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:07.280
<i>korogaru youni gamushara ni hashitta</i>

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>"What's waiting ahead?"</i>

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>nani ga matteru no?</i>

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:17.670
<i>The headwinds told me</i>

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:17.670
<i>mukaikaze ga oshiete kuretanda</i>

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>"Just believe and move forward"</i>

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>shinjite susume</i>

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:24.380
<i>The bitter taste of defeat is a seed</i>

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:24.380
<i>yaburete shitta kuyashisa wa tane</i>

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:27.010
<i>It will eventually sprout
And become your wings</i>

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:27.010
<i>yagate mebuki hane to naru</i>

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:30.850
<i>I knock on those doors</i>

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:30.850
<i>sono tobira tataku riyuu</i>

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:36.690
<i>Because the present shapes the future</i>

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:36.690
<i>ima ga mirai wo tsukuru kara</i>

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:38.980
<i>If you want to find a rainbow</i>

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:38.980
<i>niji wo mitsuketai nara</i>

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>You must lift your face</i>

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>kao wo agenakuchatte</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:47.400
<i>The hands that reached out to us
Make us much stronger</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:47.400
<i>sashidasareta te ga
bokura wo zutto tsuyoku suru</i>

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:49.490
<i>If you want to catch your dreams</i>

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:49.490
<i>yume wo tsukamitai nara</i>

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:52.780
<i>Though the step forward is unsteady</i>

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:52.780
<i>furueru sono ippo mae ni</i>

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:55.540
<i>Try and take it</i>

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:55.540
<i>fumi dashite goran yo</i>

00:22:55.660 --> 00:23:00.540
<i>Because you can surely fly now</i>

00:22:55.660 --> 00:23:00.540
<i>ima nara kitto sora mo toberu kara</i>

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:04.970
<i>Taichi crosses the sea
where the vicious Digimon lives.</i>

00:23:04.970 --> 00:23:08.280
<i>A new boy appears to face this danger.</i>

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:11.820
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"That Boy Is Joe Kido"</i>

00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:14.520
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
